// Ch7 B09, the optional side scene "The Empty Moorings" (docs/kb/story/beats/act1_ch07.md §4).
// Oruvel's moorings under the Bell's skirt on the river side: six empty iron rings in the timber, in
// the Bell's shade, the drop's bound light on the water (R08 wide; R09 low at the rings, with inserts
// on Asha's hand on the iron and the band being tied). Opened by talking to Tavi at his boat after
// B07. Tavi names the boats, Rhen names the people who sailed them, and Asha kneels at each ring,
// touches the iron, and says each name back once. No song: Cantors sing only the Hush, and this isn't
// that. The naming belongs to Reefball, not the Order; Asha leads nothing but it. The last ring was
// the Gull's: Tavi can't name it, and Rhen says it for him, and ties Pio's side-band to the ring
// (naming him with the others is accepting what "hasn't come back" means; it is Rhen who does it).
// If Rhen kept the Pemakar leaf-boat (ch05_kept_leaf_boat) he lights its own wick from his lantern's
// burner (NEVER Kell's wick: ADR 0022 sweep-H watch) and sets it on the water at the Wicklight's
// ring; it turns once in the eddy and drifts out toward the sea, and Asha says nothing. Kerrid is
// knee-deep at the far end of the moorings, back to them; he doesn't turn. No jokes; no more than
// four lines from anyone in a row. The boat names after the Gull, the Second Mooring and the
// Wicklight, and the families, are this script's (act1_ch07.md §5.2). M4-A2P-116 C2: the families are tied to
// Noa and Old Ama, the Oruvel side the player met in the match. The chapter flow takes the band (and the
// leaf-boat) out of the bag after it.
title: ch07_empty_moorings
location: ch07/tamsule_bell_galleries
---
@letterbox on
@camera R08
@music oruvel_theme fade=2.0
@mark tavi tavi_boat
@mark kerrid kerrid_far
@mark rhen rhen_moorings walk
@mark asha asha_ring_1 walk
@wait 1.5
Tavi [worried]: Would you bless them? The moorings. Gran would want it done by somebody proper. #line:ch07_moor_001
Asha [sad]: I'm not a priest, Tavi. #line:ch07_moor_002
Tavi [neutral]: You're the Cantor. #line:ch07_moor_003
Asha [tender]: Then I'll do it the way we do it at home. Tell me what tied up here. #line:ch07_moor_004
@camera R09
Tavi [neutral]: The Tallow Hen. #line:ch07_moor_005
Rhen [sad]: Ollo's. Noa's uncle, and his wife. #line:ch07_moor_006
@anim asha kneel_touch_ring
@sfx mooring_ring
Asha [tender]: Noa's uncle, and his wife. #line:ch07_moor_007
Tavi [neutral]: The Second Mooring. #line:ch07_moor_008
Rhen [sad]: The Ketters. All of them. #line:ch07_moor_009
@sfx mooring_ring
Asha [tender]: The Ketters. #line:ch07_moor_010
@mark asha asha_ring_3 walk
Tavi [sad]: The Wicklight. #line:ch07_moor_011
Rhen [grief]: Kell. #line:ch07_moor_012
@sfx mooring_ring
Asha [tender]: Kell. #line:ch07_moor_013
Tavi [neutral]: The Brass Thrush. The Low Lantern. #line:ch07_moor_014
Rhen [sad]: Ama's brothers. Old Arro and his daughter. #line:ch07_moor_015
@sfx mooring_ring
Asha [tender]: Ama's brothers. Old Arro, and his daughter. #line:ch07_moor_016
@mark asha asha_ring_6 walk
@wait 2.0
@anim tavi look_at ring_gull
@wait 2.0
@mark rhen rhen_ring_6 walk
Rhen [grief]: Pio. #line:ch07_moor_017
@wait 2.5
Tavi [grief]: ...Yes. Pio. #line:ch07_moor_018
@anim rhen untie_band
@anim rhen tie_band ring_gull
@sfx mooring_ring
@wait 1.5
Asha [tender]: Pio. #line:ch07_moor_019
@wait 1.0
Asha [tender]: Salt and stone keep you. Come up when you can. #line:ch07_moor_020
<<set $ch07_blessed_moorings = true>>
<<if $ch05_kept_leaf_boat>>
    @mark rhen rhen_moorings walk
    @anim rhen light_from_lantern
    @wait 1.5
    @anim rhen set_on_water ring_wicklight
    <<set $ch07_set_leaf_boat = true>>
    @wait 2.0
    @anim asha look_at river_mouth
    @wait 2.5
<<endif>>
@camera R08
Tavi [tender]: Thank you. #line:ch07_moor_021
@mark tavi tavi_away walk
@wait 5.0
@letterbox off
@camera release
===
